    "title": "State Grants Awarded for Social Services, White Says",
    "url": "https://www.repwhite.com/News/38738/Press-Releases/State-Grants-Awarded-for-Social-Services--White-Says",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "State Grants Awarded for Social Services, White Says\nSeptember 15, 2026\nHARRISBURG –\nAlmost $2 million in grants awarded today will support a pair of organizations helping vulnerable populations in Northeast Philadelphia, according to Rep. Martina White (R-Philadelphia).\nCaring for Friends will use a Local Share Account (LSA) grant to expand its current administrative offices and warehouse to better accommodate food that needs to be refrigerated. The $1 million will support efforts to lessen food insecurity.\nSpecial People in Northeast Inc. (SPIN) was awarded $917,450 to purchase and install generators at its facilities. The funding will support specialized residential care for the elderly and Philadelphians with disabilities.\n“The grants awarded today empower our community to take meaningful steps forward.” White said. “These investments reflect our commitment to supporting trusted organizations that lift up neighbors in need. I appreciated the opportunity to advocate for this important funding.”\nLSA grants are funded by state gaming revenue, not taxpayer dollars. The funding was approved by the Commonwealth Financing Authority (CFA). This is an independent agency that holds fiduciary responsibility over the funding of programs and investments in Pennsylvania’s economic growth.\nRepresentative Martina White\n170th District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Jennifer Fitch\n717.260.6563\njfitch@pahousegop.com\nRepWhite.com\n/\nFacebook.com/RepMartinaWhite\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": null
