    "title": "Fire, EMS Grants Awarded to Support First Responders, White Says",
    "url": "https://www.repwhite.com/News/37525/Press-Releases/Fire--EMS-Grants-Awarded-to-Support-First-Responders--White-Says",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Fire, EMS Grants Awarded to Support First Responders, White Says\nFebruary 12, 2026\nPHILADELPHIA\n– A pair of grants awarded this week in Philadelphia will support fire companies and emergency medical services as they address building projects, purchase or repair equipment, conduct training, or reduce existing debt, according to Rep. Martina White (R-Philadelphia).\nEstablished by the Legislature, the Fire and Emergency Medical Services Grant Program is administered by the Pennsylvania Emergency Management Agency and Office of the State Fire Commissioner. All funding comes from the proceeds generated by slot machine gaming.\nThe grants included $16,136 for Philadelphia Fire Department and $15,000 for Northeast First Aid Corps, commonly known as Northeast Community Ambulance.\n“All of us in Northeast Philadelphia are incredibly grateful for the tireless work of our first responders who answer the call 24/7. They are true heroes,” White said. “These grants will assist them in tackling needed projects.”\nRepresentative Martina White\n170th District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Jennifer Fitch\n717.260.6563\njfitch@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
